The '''Maridun system''' was a remote [[star system]] located in the [[Rolion sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]], and contained the [[planet]] [[Maridun]],<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> which was [[orbit]]ed by a single [[Maridun's star|star]].<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> Situated at grid square Q-6 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="Appendix" /> the Maridun system was part of neutral [[Realspace|space]] during the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />

At some point doing during the Clone Wars, several members of the [[Lurmen]] [[species]] fled their home planet [[Mygeeto]] to the Maridun system, where they hoped to find solace from the battling.<ref name="BMF 88">{{BuildFalconCite|88|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> Later in [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{HelmetCollectionCite|30|Highlights of the Saga}} places the events of "[[Cloak of Darkness]]" in [[21 BBY]]. ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' similarly dates "[[Blue Shadow Virus (episode)|Blue Shadow Virus]]" to 21 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]]. As the episode "[[Defenders of Peace]]" takes place between these two episodes according to {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}}, the episode must also take place in 21 BBY.</ref> Maridun was invaded<ref name="BMF 88" /> by the [[Separatist Droid Army]] led by [[Neimoidian]] [[General]] [[Lok Durd]], who had sought to test a new [[Defoliator|weapon]] on the planetary wildlife, including the Lurmen.<ref name="Defenders of Peace" /> However, Republic forces, who had crash-landed on the planet from a previous [[Battle of Quell|battle]],<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> helped to [[Defense of Maridun|protect]] the Lurmen from being wiped out, resulting in the destruction of the weapon and the capture of Durd.<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Maridun system first appeared in "[[Jedi Crash]],"<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> the thirteenth episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]] of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series, which aired on [[January 16]], [[2009]].<ref name="Jedi Crash Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode013.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Jedi Crash}}</ref> The system was later first identified in the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''.<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> The [[Maridun system/Legends|Maridun system]] was originally first identified in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity in ''[[The Essential Atlas]]'', a reference book authored by [[Jason Fry]] and [[Daniel Wallace]], and published on [[August 18]], 2009.<ref name="TEA">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

